 *  =========================================================================== 
 *     DETAIL DATASET FOR HE I       VERSION 1.02       21/07/87                
 *                        ( 'HOT STAR' VERSION )                                
 *                                                                              
 *         PLUS COPY OF ARTEMIO'S HE II ATOM                                    
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *  =========================================================================== 
 *     V100   RELEASED 03/09/86                                                 
 *            ADAPTED FROM KEITH BUTLER'S FILE 'HEIATOM/UH101BB'                
 *                                             (VERSION OF 27/08/86)            
 *            HOT STAR VERSION                                                  
 *                                                                              
 *     V101   RELEASED 05/12/86                                                 
 *            INCLUDING A 'FIX' KEYWORD TO KEEP HE II AND HE III POP'S FIXED.   
 *                                                                              
 *     V102   RELEASED XX/07/87                                                 
 *            INCLUDING NEW OSCILLATOR STRENGTHS AND COLLISION STRENGTHS FROM   
 *            BERRINGTON AND KINGSTON 1987                                      
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (4-5-93) BY E. SANTOLAYA. NO LEVELS 'X' NOR 'S' ARE CONSIDERED  
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (11-5-93) BY E. SANTOLAYA. LYMANN LINES IN HE II INCLUDED       
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (9-10-94) BY E. SANTOLAYA. NEW CONTINUUM FREQS. INCLUDED        
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (4-11-94) BY E. SANTOLAYA. LAST TWO LEVELS OF HEII ARE          
 *          REMOVED TO COMPARE WITH GABLER'S RESULTS                            
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (23-01-01) BY A. JOKUTHY ; ADDED LEVELS 11-20 FOR               
 *                                         HYDROGEN                             
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (27-01-01) BY A. JOKUTHY ; NEW HEI MODEL                        
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (14-03-01) BY A. JOKUTHY ; NEW HEII MODEL                       
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (July 2009) BY J. RIVERO;                                       
 *            NII   50 levels from DETAIL (Becker & Butler 1989)                
 *            NIII  41 levels (40 from WMBASIC + 1 from DETAIL)                 
 *            NIV   50 levels from WMBASIC                                      
 *            NV    27 levels form WMBASIC                                      
 *                                                                              
 *            NIII   =>  Updated electric dipole transitions (doublet and       
 *                       quartet system) from NIST database where possible      
 *                       OPACITY data ionization/recombination (includes DR)    
 *                       Collision strengths levels N31 to N312 from Stafford   
 *                       et al 1993                                             
 *                       For certain levels, we use the DR data from WM-Basic   
 *                       In this case, we have to use consistent RBF data as    
 *                       well                                                   
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (20-11-09) BY J. RIVERO;                                        
 *            NIV   =>   Updated electric dipole transitions (singlet and       
 *                       triplet system) from NIST database where possible      
 *                       OPACITY data ionization/recombination (includes DR)    
 *                       Collision strengths levels N41 to N412 from            
 *                       Ramsbottom et al 1994                                  
 *                       alternative dielectronic recombination data from WMBASI
 *                       data (commented out)                                   
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (7-07-10) BY J. RIVERO;                                         
 *          NII    =>    Updated f-value transition 23S1P - 23P1D from Kurucz   
 *                       database. We add some important intercombination       
 *                       transitions to those levels from WM-basic database.    
 *                                                                              
 *          NIII   =>    Updated f-value from transition N321 - N334 from       
 *                       OPACITY project database.                              
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *     MODIFIED (23-05-23) BY J.P ; UPDATED CARBON MODEL                        
 *                                                                              
 *     Adi's Oxygen model, and "old" Si-Model                                   
 *                                                                              
 *     Oct 23: few additional changes BY J.P:                                   
 *     f-values consistent with LINES_CnewNOSi_new_coll.dat                     
 *                                                                              
 *******************************************************************************
 *******************************************************************************
