 *                                                                              
 *  ----------------------------------                                          
 *  DEFINITION OF ATOM C                                                        
 *                                                                              
 *  CII model atom ::  Nieva & Przybilla (2008, A&A,481,199)                    
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *  Miguel A. Urbaneja - Last revision 2023.05.12                               
 *  Comments :: VERSION 1.0 for FASTWIND APRIL 2023                             
 *  Comments :: The original labels for the levels have been                    
 *     modified to avoid potential issues with other ions/atoms                 
 *                                                                              
 *  CIII/CIV model atom ::                                                      
 *                                                                              
 *  older version from Luiz Carneiro (around 2016),                             
 *  updated by JP (CIII) and Carlos Martinez-Sebastian (CIV) (Spring 2023)      
 *                                                                              
 *  The model atom (CIII-CIV) is a merge of three different databases           
 *  NIST, Adi's and TOP_base (The opacity project database).                    
 *  The levels order follows the ordering chosen in most of the database.       
 *  As the CBB data was taken from Przybilla's carbon model, a special          
 *  attention was invested to follow also Pryzybilla's levels labeling.         
 *  The order finally chosen mostly agrees with Adis and TOP_base.              
 *  In the cases where this last sentence is not true, care has been taken      
 *  to adress the record corresponding to the actual labeled level              
 *  (see RBF records ordering). RBB transitions were taken from NIST when       
 *  present. RBB transitions not present in NIST (possibly not observed         
 *  or not allowed transitions) were taken from Adi's carbon model.             
 *  CBF data were taken from Adi's (for the levels present in both              
 *  detail files, this and Adis file) and from NAHAR                            
 *  (http://www.astronomy.ohio-state.edu/~nahar/nahar_radiativeatomicdata/index.
 *  for the levels not present in Adi's data. The CBF data from TOP_base        
 *  is also commented aside the value presently used.                           
 *  That shows the good agreement between independet databases.                 
 *                                                                              
 *  General order of levels (and also their energies) follows NIST database.    
 *  However, once the CBB data was taken from Pryzibilla's model, some levels   
 *  which had similar (or almost equal) energies, had their orders inverted     
 *  to follow Pryzibilla's level ordering. (C3_39,C3_40;C3_50,C3_51)            
 *                                                                              
 *  After completing a new model atom remember that when looking into           
 *  nlte_dim.f90 there must have a difference of 24 levels between RBF          
 *  transitions and CBS + CBF transitions. This difference of 24 levels         
 *  comes uniquely from the He model atom.                                      
 *                                                                              
 *  ATTENTION: dimes.eo does not accept 1.00e+10, only 1.00E+10 (upper case E). 
 *                                                                              
 *  MODIFIED VERISON BY CMS (24-03-23)                                          
 *                                                                              
 *                                                                              
 *  -----------------------------------------------------------------------     
 *  CARBON ATOM                                                                 
 *  -----------------------------------------------------------------------     
 *  Label Z   Ato.Weight   Number Fraction of the elem. (Asplund 2009)          
